From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally map the render notifier
 records ASC-cached

g16_notifier_cached=1 (load time, default 0) gives the render graph's TA
and FS notifier records their own session page in the ASC-cached class,
the attribute index macOS uses for its per-queue objects. The work
records name that page at +0x10 and +0x20. The service stamps at +0x620
and +0x630, which the host reads to retire a render, stay in the
uncached notifier page, and so do the threshold cells the host writes.

The firmware cleans and invalidates a record when it prepares the
record's stage and in the scan's equality branch. The host never writes
a record after init. It reads the record CONTEXT words only for a
render with nothing published behind it. A CONTEXT read older than the
firmware's holds that render: only a later render published behind it,
or the completion deadline, which fail-stops the device, ends the hold.
The next commit adds the word that retires such a render without
CONTEXT. The page is never dropped, so no cached mapping is torn down
at client exit.

The stats file gains a notifier_cached line, and the boot log has one
line when the switch is on. Value 0 behaves as before. Values other
than 0 and 1 act as 0: the split records of the experimental line
(value 2) are not supported on this kernel.

This is the release-line port of the experimental-line commit of the
same title.

Assisted-by: LLM
